program            = 003_storage_class_linkage
area               = 10_declarations_and_types
description        = Storage class and linkage in one translation unit: file-scope static, extern declared then defined here, block-scope static persistence, static function, static-duration zero initialization
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every object read is either explicitly initialized or has static storage duration and is
therefore zero initialized by the standard. zero_init_probe is a static-duration int with no
initializer, so reading it is well defined and yields zero; it is never left in an
indeterminate state. shared_counter, file_static and the block-scope static total all have
static storage duration and explicit initializers. All arithmetic is on small int values far
from the int range edges, so there is no signed overflow: the largest intermediate value is
103. No shift and no pointer arithmetic is performed. No object is modified twice between
sequence points. Critically, the three accumulate calls each mutate the block-scope static
object total, so they are made on three separate statements and assigned to three distinct
locals before any printf runs -- no printf call receives more than one side-effecting
argument, so the output cannot depend on unspecified evaluation order. The internal_triple
call inside a printf is pure and mutates nothing. There is no aliasing violation: every
object is accessed only through an lvalue of its own declared type. No padding byte is read.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This program prints no size and no alignment at all, so the measured i686 width differences
(4-byte long and pointer versus 8 bytes on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64) cannot surface. All
printed values are small int quantities. No address or pointer value is printed. Plain char
is not used, so the measured char signedness difference (signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned
on aarch64 and riscv64) is irrelevant. The only printf conversion specifier used in the
program is %d.

Single translation unit note: the suite compiles exactly one source file per cell, so there
is no second translation unit to link against. External linkage is therefore exercised the
only standard-conforming way available in one file -- extern int shared_counter; is declared
first and then satisfied by the definition int shared_counter = 41; later in the same
translation unit. Block-scope static storage duration is exercised by calling accumulate
three times and observing that the value persists: total starts at 100, becomes 101, then
103, then stays 103 because the third call adds zero. The repeated 103 in the golden output
is the assertion that the object persisted rather than being re-initialized on each entry; a
compiler that re-initialized it would print 101 102 100 instead.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
file_static=7
extern_defined_here=42
block_static_accum=101 103 103
static_fn=21
zero_init=0
END
